"""@@NAME@@: run the numbered steps in order, into one run folder.

From this folder: bash run.sh <slug>   (makes outputs/run_<YYYYMMDD>_<slug>/ and its RUN.txt, then runs this file)
Without run.sh:   snakemake -s @@DEST@@/Snakefile --cores 4 --config run=run_YYYYMMDD_<slug>
One step:         add the rule name, e.g. step01_prepare
Interpreters:     @@ENV_NOTE@@; override with --config rscript=/path/to/Rscript python=/path/to/python jupyter=/path/to/jupyter quarto=/path/to/quarto

Step scripts live in code/; paths are relative to this folder. Every output, log, benchmark and executed
notebook of a step goes under outputs/<run>/ (OUT below); logs and benchmarks under outputs/<run>/logs/.
A qmd step's page goes to reports/site/. Wrap an output in protected() once it is expensive to recompute.
"""

